N5008 [dcl.init.aggr]/4.2, [dcl.init.general]/16.6.2.2 (C++20): the
elements of `agg a(3, 4)' are copy-initialized; the element of class type
`conv' is constructed from 3.  The parenthesized aggregate initialization
assigned to the member instead (operator= of a converted temporary,
"member 'conv::operator=' is not accessible" for the deleted one, bin53).
Found from libc++'s __tuple_leaf (tuple:469).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18
accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
